urse experiences start with  great content but most importantly what  we see is that experiences are powered  by data right and that's where machine  learning and AI plays a very  increasingly important role so just to  give you a flavor on behalf of our  brands we collect a large amount of data  so we as I said power websites apps  social media advertising videos all of  that data plus we get other brands to  give us other data maybe visits to their  physical branch offices or to their  calls to the call center in addition we  deliver a lot of content you deliver a  lot of experiences in the digital side  so together this creates a vast pool of  data so what what essentially is  happening is that this always on always  connected consumer is also creating a  lot of data for us which can then be  used to deliver to their great expect to  their big expectations right  are you provide sort of a IML as a  software service model yeah for their  customers in their business how much  that dinner passes to your platform yes  so the data belongs to the brands we are  the operator that in the sense we  collect the data on their behalf we help  analyze and understand and we help them  deliver the experiences through the  channels that we offer them services  against so we have an analytics product  which collects the data through tracking  mechanisms we have mechanisms where they  can transfer data to us we have audience  Manager which allows them to manage  their customer profiles we have various  delivery mechanisms so we have service  that enables people to create and  personalize their websites through  testing recommendations personalization  we have the ability to send emails and  notifications so we allow their digital  marketers to figure out how to run their  email campaigns their mobile app  notifications as well as the various  acquisition channels that they use like  Facebook or Google or the display ad  networks through which they acquire  customers so all of these things we are  doing on behalf of the brand in that  sense it's very different from the  googles and Facebooks of the world where  they are trying to optimize revenue that  they generating on their properties we  are enabling sort of the other side  which is enabling the branch to figure  out how to use their data to run  effective marketing and advertising  campaigns across these different  channels that they touch their consumers  Consulting yes we do it more as a SAS  model we work with other partners if  they want to create consulting practices  on on top of it but we what we sell is  SAS solutions  so so this data that I talked about is  large right it is high dimensional it's  also real time in the sense it's  constantly coming in at very high speeds  and to take that data make sense out of  it make predictions based on it and then  actually act against it is what we call  the experience intelligence right so  that's that's what that's what my group  is responsible for driving so to  simplify it what what we are doing with  this data is taking this data and  enabling the brands to get intelligent  insights who are my consumers what are  they doing what do they want what what  is the so to describe experience in a  nutshell it would be figuring out what  content to show which consumer in a  specific context right so the right  thing the right content at the right  place to the right person bringing that  together as the experience and taking a  whole amount of data that comes from  experiences and then creating that  intelligent insights into who the  consumer is what what's the different  content that they they are engaging with  and what is the context and channel  through which they are engaging with  with that content and then using it  enabling it to be used for designing  campaigns designing marketing and  advertising campaigns and actually  delivering the campaign is is what what  we are enabling  so I will get you get into one example  of how this works and maybe we can then  dig deeper into how to generalize it but  that's sort of in a nutshell what what  we are trying to do so let's look at the  experience when you go to a website like  CNN and then there is this slot here  where you want to show something right  now behind this behind this particular  slot out there there's a whole complex  ecosystem of systems and decisions that  decides what's going to what's going to  show up there  so CNN will of course when the person  comes through a browser or through  through a mobile phone to this website  CNN will of course deliver the page with  all the news and other stuff but what  happens in this this particular slot is  that there is an ad tag this ad tag  calls supply-side platform which is  think of supply-side platform as  something which is helping the publisher  figure out which among the different ads  it should be showing in that particular  particular particular slot so the supply  side platform connects with a large  number of demand side demand-side  platforms which are essentially  aggregators of advertisers who are  trying to show their ad in this  particular slot so you might have Ford  or you might have Citibank and you might  have Nordstrom all of them want to that  gets displayed or have their ad  displayed in in this in this particular  slot the supply side form platform is  just enabling these different people to  come back with a bid and an ad to be  shown in that particular spot  so these different demand-side platforms  will come back with a response in which  there is a bid which indicates I am  willing to pay this much for an  impression to be shown to this  particular person on this in this  particular slot and the supply side  platform will run an auction which takes  all the bids figure out the highest bid  and whoever wins that bid it will direct  to the winning ad server so say the  first ad server was a winning one so it  gets redirected the ad server request  gets redirected to tha