 set of information that  you can then connect with that that  identity to get a richer in profile for  that user but there are some things  which you have to predict which is how  likely that person is going to engage  with an offer for a fixed for a CD with  a certain percentage of interest or what  likely like likelihood is that person  interest in a certain kind of content or  a certain kind of credit card so that's  that's what falls into the bucket of the  customer intelligence which we have to  take the data that we have and then  based on that build these predictions  the I don't have much time but I'll  quickly go into a couple more things  which is these things don't happen in  silos these experiences  I showed are part of a bigger customer  journey the customer might interact with  the brand's through multiple different  touch points before ending ending up  making a purchase and the understanding  of the journey is as important as  understanding of these individual  experiences so journey design is one of  the critical things that many brands and  marketers spend a lot of effort in in  order to figure out how to connect a  bunch of experiences to give that  customer a nice smooth experience  towards getting them to a specific  outcome and in this journey optimization  you have several decisions that you end  up making what is the offer that I  should show that person what is the best  time to send an email to that person  what is the call center script that I  should serve that person which channel  should I reach the customer through  should I send them something through an  app should I send them something through  an SMS message or something through an  email all of these decisions you need  tools to help figure out what is the  best mechanism in order to make that  journey smooth and easy for the for the  end consumer  so I guess I don't have much time but so  these things play also a role in the  return on investment for advertising  that people tha